  ($c$americano$c$, $c$Espresso topped up with hot water. Black coffee, lighter than espresso.$c$, $c$Strong coffee topped up with hot water: a big mug of black coffee that tastes close to filter coffee.$c$),
  ($c$macchiato$c$, $c$Espresso with a small dot of milk foam. Not the same as a caramel macchiato.$c$, $c$A tiny strong coffee with just a spoon of milk foam on top. Mostly coffee. Not the big sweet caramel one.$c$),
  ($c$cortado$c$, $c$Espresso cut with an equal splash of warm milk. Stronger than a flat white.$c$, $c$Strong coffee and warm milk, half and half, in a small glass. Stronger than most milky coffees.$c$),
  ($c$flat_white$c$, $c$A double espresso with a little silky milk and very thin foam. Stronger and smaller than a latte.$c$, $c$A double strong coffee with a little silky hot milk and a very thin foam, in a small cup. You taste the coffee more than the milk.$c$),
